      "foundedYear": 1875,
      "parentCompany": null,
      "shortDescription": "MANNESMANN DEMAG is the industrial pneumatic-technology brand manufactured by MD Drucklufttechnik in Renningen, Germany. Its range covers air motors, pneumatic and electric grinding spindles, robot deburring spindles, chipping hammers, chisels, screwdriving tools and other professional air tools.",
      "fullDescription": [
        "Official company sources trace the business behind MANNESMANN DEMAG to Gendebien & Nauman OHG, founded in 1875, and document its later operation through FMA, DEMAG and Mannesmann Demag. The air-tools and air-motors division was transferred to Strohm Karl Gänssle in 1984 and was renamed MD Drucklufttechnik GmbH & Co. KG in 2009. Development, production, assembly and service are now based in Renningen, Germany.",
        "The current product programme includes pneumatic motors, grinding spindles, electric grinding and brush drives, robot deburring spindles, chipping hammers and tampers, chisels, screwdriving tools and pneumatic tools for grinding, drilling, brushing, countersinking and filing. Official application pages position these technologies for automation, machinery and plant engineering, metal and surface processing, foundries, construction, assembly work and stone processing."
      ],
