      "shortDescription": "Riedel develops and manufactures transformers, inductive components, power supplies and complete industrial energy-supply systems. The AQ Riedel portfolio includes single- and three-phase transformers, chokes, DC supplies and battery chargers, AC and DC UPS modules, variable transformers, enclosures and power-distribution cabinets.",
      "fullDescription": [
        "Riedel was founded in 1972 by Michael and Peter Riedel and operates from Ilshofen-Eckartshausen, Germany. Official company sources identify the current legal entity as AQ Riedel Trafobau GmbH after AQ Group AB completed its acquisition of Michael Riedel Transformatorenbau GmbH. The business continues to develop and manufacture inductive components, transformers, power supplies and complete energy-supply systems at its German production site.",
        "The documented range covers custom single- and three-phase transformers, line and motor chokes, sine and motor filters, primary-switched power supplies, battery chargers, AC and DC uninterruptible power supplies, variable-ratio transformers, enclosures and power-distribution systems. Riedel lists applications in mechanical engineering, railway and drive technology, medical and semiconductor equipment, food production, building automation, automotive systems, maritime equipment and test systems."
