      "shortDescription": "NORD DRIVESYSTEMS develops and manufactures modular mechanical and electronic drive technology. Its portfolio combines gear units and geared motors, industrial gear units, electric motors, frequency inverters and motor starters for centralised and decentralised drive systems.",
      "fullDescription": [
        "Getriebebau NORD GmbH & Co. KG was founded in Bargteheide near Hamburg in 1965 and remains headquartered there. Official NORD sources describe the group as a system provider for mechanical and electronic drive technology, supported by its own manufacturing of gear units, motors and drive electronics and an international production, assembly and service network.",
        "NORD's modular portfolio covers helical, parallel-shaft, bevel and worm geared motors, MAXXDRIVE industrial gear units, synchronous and asynchronous electric motors, and NORDAC frequency inverters and motor starters for cabinet-based and decentralised installation. Documented solution families include DuoDrive, LogiDrive, UNICASE and NORDBLOC.1 systems for material handling, intralogistics, food and beverage production, mixing and agitation, bulk handling and other industrial applications."
      ],
